.TH WEBDOC-PIPE 1 "2025-10-01" "v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webdoc-pipe \- Serve piped HTML/CSS/JS as three HTTP files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webdoc-pipe open
.br
.B webdoc-pipe url
.br
.B webdoc-pipe stop
.br
.B webdoc-pipe html
.br
.B webdoc-pipe css
.br
.B webdoc-pipe js
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBwebdoc-pipe\fR maintains an in-memory web document and serves it via HTTP at:
.IP
http://127.0.0.1:PORT/
.PP
It serves exactly three files:
.RS
.IP \[bu] 2
\fI/\fR or \fI/index.html\fR → HTML content
.IP \[bu] 2
\fI/style.css\fR → CSS content
.IP \[bu] 2
\fI/script.js\fR → JavaScript content
.RE
.PP
Content is updated by piping to subcommands:
.IP
cat index.html | webdoc-pipe html
.PP
The daemon starts automatically and runs per-user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBopen\fR
Open the document in Firefox (or \fCxdg-open\fR).
.TP
\fBurl\fR
Print the document URL.
.TP
\fBstop\fR
Stop the daemon.
.TP
\fBhtml\fR
Read stdin as HTML (served as \fI/index.html\fR).
.TP
\fBcss\fR
Read stdin as CSS (served as \fI/style.css\fR).
.TP
\fBjs\fR
Read stdin as JavaScript (served as \fI/script.js\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/webdoc-pipe-*.sock\fR
Unix domain socket.
.TP
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/webdoc-pipe.current\fR
Daemon metadata (PID, port, socket path).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBWEBDOC_BROWSER\fR
Browser command (default: \fCfirefox\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
firefox(1), xdg-open(1)
